1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,293
In February twenty twenty-six,

2
00:00:02,293 --> 00:00:05,428
more than four hundred fifty thousand Ram

3
00:00:05,428 --> 00:00:08,180
and Jeep owners got a warning nobody

4
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:10,397
expects from a truck company:

5
00:00:10,397 --> 00:00:11,238
do not tow.

6
00:00:11,418 --> 00:00:14,440
A faulty module could leave trailers with

7
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:15,619
no turn signals,

8
00:00:15,619 --> 00:00:16,798
no brake lights,

9
00:00:16,798 --> 00:00:19,377
and in some cases no trailer brakes

10
00:00:19,377 --> 00:00:19,893
at all.

11
00:00:20,073 --> 00:00:22,044
And that recall is only one of

12
00:00:22,044 --> 00:00:24,410
the ways towing can go wrong without

13
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:26,052
the driver ever noticing.

14
00:00:26,402 --> 00:00:28,820
Towing is one of the main reasons

15
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,431
Americans buy pickups.

16
00:00:30,611 --> 00:00:32,611
But it is also where trucks get

17
00:00:32,611 --> 00:00:32,933
hurt.

18
00:00:33,113 --> 00:00:35,721
Overloaded beds, wrong hitches,

19
00:00:35,721 --> 00:00:39,592
overheated transmissions and swaying trailers.

20
00:00:39,772 --> 00:00:41,923
In this video we go through nine

21
00:00:41,923 --> 00:00:44,209
towing mistakes that wreck trucks,

22
00:00:44,209 --> 00:00:46,899
with the 2026 lessons every owner should

23
00:00:46,899 --> 00:00:49,118
know before hooking up a trailer.

24
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:51,842
This is general safety information,

25
00:00:51,842 --> 00:00:54,692
not a replacement for your owner's manual,

26
00:00:54,692 --> 00:00:56,999
which is always the final word for

27
00:00:56,999 --> 00:00:57,745
your truck.

28
00:00:57,925 --> 00:00:59,810
Every number we use comes from a

29
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,931
published source in the description.

30
00:01:02,111 --> 00:01:04,258
If we could not confirm a figure,

31
00:01:04,258 --> 00:01:05,234
we left it out.

32
00:01:05,414 --> 00:01:06,842
Let's start with that recall.

33
00:01:07,191 --> 00:01:09,776
According to Pickup Truck Talk,

34
00:01:09,776 --> 00:01:13,612
Chrysler filed safety recall twenty-six V zero

35
00:01:13,612 --> 00:01:17,365
five nine with federal regulators on February

36
00:01:17,365 --> 00:01:19,533
second, twenty twenty-six.

37
00:01:19,713 --> 00:01:22,661
It covered four hundred fifty-six thousand,

38
00:01:22,661 --> 00:01:24,992
two hundred eighty-seven vehicles,

39
00:01:24,992 --> 00:01:28,351
including more than three hundred twelve thousand

40
00:01:28,351 --> 00:01:29,790
Ram fifteen hundreds,

41
00:01:29,790 --> 00:01:33,698
almost ninety-seven thousand Ram twenty-five hundreds and

42
00:01:33,698 --> 00:01:37,126
more than thirty thousand Ram thirty-five hundreds

43
00:01:37,126 --> 00:01:40,485
from the twenty twenty-five and twenty twenty-six

44
00:01:40,485 --> 00:01:41,307
model years.

45
00:01:41,657 --> 00:01:44,053
The problem was the trailer brake and

46
00:01:44,053 --> 00:01:45,477
towing control module.

47
00:01:45,657 --> 00:01:47,250
According to the report,

48
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:49,706
trailer turn signals might not flash,

49
00:01:49,706 --> 00:01:52,295
trailer stop lamps might not light when

50
00:01:52,295 --> 00:01:54,153
braking, and trailer brakes,

51
00:01:54,153 --> 00:01:56,211
where equipped, might not work.

52
00:01:56,391 --> 00:01:58,604
Owners were told not to tow until

53
00:01:58,604 --> 00:02:00,214
the module was replaced,

54
00:02:00,214 --> 00:02:01,220
free of charge.

55
00:02:01,570 --> 00:02:03,370
Here is the first twist.

56
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:05,768
Many drivers would never notice.

57
00:02:05,948 --> 00:02:08,108
You cannot see your trailer lights from

58
00:02:08,108 --> 00:02:09,105
the driver's seat.

59
00:02:09,285 --> 00:02:11,671
That leads us to mistake number one,

60
00:02:11,671 --> 00:02:13,989
the simplest and most common one of

61
00:02:13,989 --> 00:02:14,255
all.

62
00:02:14,604 --> 00:02:15,937
Mistake number one:

63
00:02:15,937 --> 00:02:17,902
skipping the pre-trip check.

64
00:02:18,082 --> 00:02:22,009
The National Association of Trailer Manufacturers recommends

65
00:02:22,009 --> 00:02:24,430
checking that the brakes work on both

66
00:02:24,430 --> 00:02:26,132
the truck and the trailer,

67
00:02:26,132 --> 00:02:28,161
checking tire pressure on both,

68
00:02:28,161 --> 00:02:29,535
including the spares,

69
00:02:29,535 --> 00:02:31,761
and making sure the wheel lug nuts

70
00:02:31,761 --> 00:02:34,510
are tightened to the correct torque before

71
00:02:34,510 --> 00:02:35,230
every trip.

72
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:37,449
And check the lights every time.

73
00:02:37,629 --> 00:02:40,308
Have someone stand behind the trailer while

74
00:02:40,308 --> 00:02:41,928
you test the turn signals,

75
00:02:41,928 --> 00:02:43,921
brake lights and running lights.

76
00:02:44,101 --> 00:02:45,225
If you are alone,

77
00:02:45,225 --> 00:02:47,737
some trucks have a trailer light check

78
00:02:47,737 --> 00:02:50,118
feature, or you can use a reflection

79
00:02:50,118 --> 00:02:51,241
in a shop window.

80
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:53,412
It takes two minutes and it can

81
00:02:53,412 --> 00:02:54,440
prevent a crash.

82
00:02:54,790 --> 00:02:56,427
And check for recalls.

83
00:02:56,607 --> 00:03:00,231
You can enter your vehicle identification number

84
00:03:00,231 --> 00:03:01,439
on the N H T S A

85
00:03:01,439 --> 00:03:03,554
website to see open recalls,

86
00:03:03,554 --> 00:03:05,819
as the Ram owners were told to

87
00:03:05,819 --> 00:03:06,045
do.

88
00:03:06,225 --> 00:03:07,688
Do the same for your trailer.

89
00:03:07,868 --> 00:03:09,535
A recall is free to fix,

90
00:03:09,535 --> 00:03:11,618
but only if you know about it.

91
00:03:11,969 --> 00:03:13,296
Mistake number two:

92
00:03:13,296 --> 00:03:15,463
trusting the big towing number.

93
00:03:15,643 --> 00:03:18,678
Truck ads love to show maximum towing

94
00:03:18,678 --> 00:03:19,416
capacity.

95
00:03:19,596 --> 00:03:22,628
But that number usually applies to a

96
00:03:22,628 --> 00:03:26,586
specific configuration, often a particular cab,

97
00:03:26,586 --> 00:03:30,208
bed, engine, axle ratio and towing package.

98
00:03:30,388 --> 00:03:32,034
The truck on the lot may be

99
00:03:32,034 --> 00:03:33,070
rated much lower.

100
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:34,721
Here is the twist:

101
00:03:34,721 --> 00:03:37,469
towing capacity is often not the limit

102
00:03:37,469 --> 00:03:38,481
you hit first.

103
00:03:38,661 --> 00:03:39,985
Payload is.

104
00:03:40,165 --> 00:03:42,668
Payload is how much weight your truck

105
00:03:42,668 --> 00:03:44,832
can carry, including passengers,

106
00:03:44,832 --> 00:03:45,982
cargo in the bed,

107
00:03:45,982 --> 00:03:49,026
and the trailer's tongue weight pressing down

108
00:03:49,026 --> 00:03:49,906
on the hitch.

109
00:03:50,086 --> 00:03:51,346
A family of four,

110
00:03:51,346 --> 00:03:53,644
a cooler, some gear and a heavy

111
00:03:53,644 --> 00:03:56,388
trailer tongue can use up the payload

112
00:03:56,388 --> 00:03:59,501
long before you reach the towing capacity.

113
00:03:59,852 --> 00:04:02,383
Your truck's payload is printed on a

114
00:04:02,383 --> 00:04:04,774
sticker on the driver's door jamb.

115
00:04:04,954 --> 00:04:07,563
It is specific to that exact truck,

116
00:04:07,563 --> 00:04:09,203
including its options.

117
00:04:09,383 --> 00:04:12,102
Heavier trims with more features often have

118
00:04:12,102 --> 00:04:12,924
less payload.

119
00:04:13,104 --> 00:04:15,296
Read it before you buy a trailer,

120
00:04:15,296 --> 00:04:15,961
not after.

121
00:04:16,311 --> 00:04:18,064
And there are more ratings to know.

122
00:04:18,244 --> 00:04:20,653
The gross vehicle weight rating is the

123
00:04:20,653 --> 00:04:22,238
most the truck can weigh,

124
00:04:22,238 --> 00:04:23,062
fully loaded.

125
00:04:23,242 --> 00:04:25,576
The gross combined weight rating is the

126
00:04:25,576 --> 00:04:27,730
most the truck and trailer can weigh

127
00:04:27,730 --> 00:04:28,269
together.

128
00:04:28,449 --> 00:04:30,623
And the rear axle has its own

129
00:04:30,623 --> 00:04:31,073
limit.

130
00:04:31,253 --> 00:04:33,324
Going over any one of these can

131
00:04:33,324 --> 00:04:35,862
overload brakes, tires and suspension.

132
00:04:36,212 --> 00:04:38,754
The good news is that major truck

133
00:04:38,754 --> 00:04:42,066
makers use a common industry test standard,

134
00:04:42,066 --> 00:04:44,377
called S A E J twenty-eight oh

135
00:04:44,377 --> 00:04:46,765
seven, to rate towing capacity.

136
00:04:46,945 --> 00:04:50,161
It makes ratings more comparable between brands.

137
00:04:50,341 --> 00:04:52,411
But it does not change the rule:

138
00:04:52,411 --> 00:04:54,934
stay within every rating on your truck,

139
00:04:54,934 --> 00:04:55,774
not just one.

140
00:04:56,125 --> 00:04:58,123
And the easiest way to know your

141
00:04:58,123 --> 00:05:00,434
real weights is a public truck scale,

142
00:05:00,434 --> 00:05:02,371
like those at many truck stops.

143
00:05:02,551 --> 00:05:03,624
For a small fee,

144
00:05:03,624 --> 00:05:05,638
you can weigh the truck alone,

145
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:07,114
then with the trailer,

146
00:05:07,114 --> 00:05:09,261
and see exactly where you stand.

147
00:05:09,441 --> 00:05:13,170
Many experienced towers do it before every

148
00:05:13,170 --> 00:05:13,969
big trip.

149
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:15,792
Mistake number three:

150
00:05:15,792 --> 00:05:18,035
getting the tongue weight wrong.

151
00:05:18,215 --> 00:05:20,610
Tongue weight is the downward force of

152
00:05:20,610 --> 00:05:22,185
the trailer on the hitch.

153
00:05:22,365 --> 00:05:25,979
According to the trailer manufacturers' association,

154
00:05:25,979 --> 00:05:28,203
a general rule is to place about

155
00:05:28,203 --> 00:05:30,566
sixty percent of the load ahead of

156
00:05:30,566 --> 00:05:33,415
the trailer axle and forty percent behind

157
00:05:33,415 --> 00:05:36,056
it, and check the trailer's manual for

158
00:05:36,056 --> 00:05:37,238
the exact figure.

159
00:05:37,588 --> 00:05:39,097
Here is why it matters.

160
00:05:39,277 --> 00:05:41,338
Too little weight on the tongue,

161
00:05:41,338 --> 00:05:43,399
with too much weight at the back

162
00:05:43,399 --> 00:05:44,365
of the trailer,

163
00:05:44,365 --> 00:05:46,104
is a classic cause of sway.

164
00:05:46,284 --> 00:05:48,795
Too much weight on the tongue can

165
00:05:48,795 --> 00:05:51,155
overload the truck's rear axle,

166
00:05:51,155 --> 00:05:54,275
lift the front wheels and reduce steering

167
00:05:54,275 --> 00:05:55,188
and braking.

168
00:05:55,368 --> 00:05:57,642
Either mistake makes the whole rig less

169
00:05:57,642 --> 00:05:58,050
stable.

170
00:05:58,401 --> 00:06:00,299
And here is the twist many owners

171
00:06:00,299 --> 00:06:00,990
do not know.

172
00:06:01,170 --> 00:06:03,728
Hitch maker Blue Ox recommends a weight

173
00:06:03,728 --> 00:06:06,679
distribution hitch when tongue weight is more

174
00:06:06,679 --> 00:06:08,909
than ten to fifteen percent of the

175
00:06:08,909 --> 00:06:10,418
trailer's total weight,

176
00:06:10,418 --> 00:06:12,517
when the truck sags at the rear,

177
00:06:12,517 --> 00:06:14,353
or when you are close to the

178
00:06:14,353 --> 00:06:15,206
towing limit.

179
00:06:15,386 --> 00:06:18,673
A weight distribution hitch spreads the load

180
00:06:18,673 --> 00:06:20,541
across the truck's axles.

181
00:06:20,891 --> 00:06:21,871
A simple test:

182
00:06:21,871 --> 00:06:24,112
look at your truck from the side

183
00:06:24,112 --> 00:06:25,163
after hitching.

184
00:06:25,343 --> 00:06:27,758
If the rear squats and the front

185
00:06:27,758 --> 00:06:30,173
rises, the load is not balanced.

186
00:06:30,353 --> 00:06:32,697
Measure the front fender height before and

187
00:06:32,697 --> 00:06:33,534
after hitching.

188
00:06:33,714 --> 00:06:36,423
A big change means you should adjust

189
00:06:36,423 --> 00:06:38,079
the load or the hitch.

190
00:06:38,430 --> 00:06:39,909
Mistake number four:

191
00:06:39,909 --> 00:06:42,201
not knowing what to do when the

192
00:06:42,201 --> 00:06:43,236
trailer sways.

193
00:06:43,416 --> 00:06:46,167
Sway is when the trailer starts moving

194
00:06:46,167 --> 00:06:48,339
side to side behind the truck.

195
00:06:48,519 --> 00:06:51,005
Blue Ox lists common causes:

196
00:06:51,005 --> 00:06:53,225
crosswinds, uneven loads,

197
00:06:53,225 --> 00:06:56,598
sudden maneuvers, wrong tire pressure,

198
00:06:56,598 --> 00:06:59,351
high speed and the wrong hitch.

199
00:06:59,701 --> 00:07:01,059
Here is the twist:

200
00:07:01,059 --> 00:07:03,927
the natural reaction is the wrong one.

201
00:07:04,107 --> 00:07:06,947
Slamming the brakes or jerking the wheel

202
00:07:06,947 --> 00:07:08,368
can make sway worse.

203
00:07:08,548 --> 00:07:12,041
The trailer manufacturers' association says not to

204
00:07:12,041 --> 00:07:14,137
steer into the sway and not to

205
00:07:14,137 --> 00:07:16,512
hit the accelerator or the brakes.

206
00:07:16,692 --> 00:07:19,201
Steer straight and let the rig slow

207
00:07:19,201 --> 00:07:19,560
down.

208
00:07:19,910 --> 00:07:21,841
Blue Ox adds that if your brake

209
00:07:21,841 --> 00:07:23,150
controller allows it,

210
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:25,767
applying the trailer brakes alone can help

211
00:07:25,767 --> 00:07:27,201
straighten the trailer.

212
00:07:27,381 --> 00:07:29,978
That is why a properly adjusted brake

213
00:07:29,978 --> 00:07:31,874
controller is so important.

214
00:07:32,054 --> 00:07:33,398
Once you are safe,

215
00:07:33,398 --> 00:07:35,190
stop and check the load,

216
00:07:35,190 --> 00:07:37,580
the tire pressure and the hitch.

217
00:07:37,930 --> 00:07:40,310
And prevention is better than reaction.

218
00:07:40,490 --> 00:07:42,599
Load the trailer correctly,

219
00:07:42,599 --> 00:07:45,176
keep tires at the right pressure,

220
00:07:45,176 --> 00:07:47,832
slow down in strong wind and avoid

221
00:07:47,832 --> 00:07:49,395
sudden lane changes.

222
00:07:49,575 --> 00:07:52,569
Many modern trucks also have trailer sway

223
00:07:52,569 --> 00:07:55,710
control built into their stability systems,

224
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,390
but it is a safety net,

225
00:07:57,390 --> 00:07:59,362
not a license to tow badly.

226
00:07:59,712 --> 00:08:01,550
Mistake number five:

227
00:08:01,550 --> 00:08:03,113
driving too fast.

228
00:08:03,293 --> 00:08:05,659
A truck and trailer take longer to

229
00:08:05,659 --> 00:08:07,468
stop than the truck alone,

230
00:08:07,468 --> 00:08:09,625
even if the trailer has brakes,

231
00:08:09,625 --> 00:08:13,243
according to the trailer manufacturers' association.

232
00:08:13,423 --> 00:08:14,647
The faster you go,

233
00:08:14,647 --> 00:08:16,959
the more distance you need and the

234
00:08:16,959 --> 00:08:18,659
more likely sway becomes.

235
00:08:19,009 --> 00:08:20,634
And there is a legal angle.

236
00:08:20,814 --> 00:08:23,311
According to the same association,

237
00:08:23,311 --> 00:08:26,028
many states set a fifty-five mile per

238
00:08:26,028 --> 00:08:29,405
hour speed limit for vehicles towing trailers.

239
00:08:29,585 --> 00:08:31,187
Rules differ by state,

240
00:08:31,187 --> 00:08:33,443
so check the laws where you are

241
00:08:33,443 --> 00:08:36,282
driving, especially on a long road trip

242
00:08:36,282 --> 00:08:37,956
through several states.

243
00:08:38,306 --> 00:08:41,053
Here is a twist many people miss:

244
00:08:41,053 --> 00:08:42,218
trailer tires.

245
00:08:42,398 --> 00:08:45,102
Many trailer tires have lower speed ratings

246
00:08:45,102 --> 00:08:46,926
than the tires on your truck.

247
00:08:47,106 --> 00:08:49,962
Driving faster than the tire is rated

248
00:08:49,962 --> 00:08:53,050
for can cause heat buildup and blowouts.

249
00:08:53,230 --> 00:08:55,703
The rating is printed on the sidewall.

250
00:08:55,883 --> 00:08:57,544
Check it before your next trip.

251
00:08:57,894 --> 00:09:00,343
And the fuel bill rises with speed.

252
00:09:00,523 --> 00:09:03,295
Towing already uses a lot more fuel,

253
00:09:03,295 --> 00:09:06,452
and air resistance grows quickly as speed

254
00:09:06,452 --> 00:09:07,222
increases.

255
00:09:07,402 --> 00:09:10,476
With diesel at six dollars and twenty-eight

256
00:09:10,476 --> 00:09:12,549
cents a gallon in the week of

257
00:09:12,549 --> 00:09:15,265
October nineteenth, twenty twenty-six,

258
00:09:15,265 --> 00:09:18,911
according to the Energy Information Administration,

259
00:09:18,911 --> 00:09:21,056
slowing down saves real money.

260
00:09:21,406 --> 00:09:22,932
Mistake number six:

261
00:09:22,932 --> 00:09:24,459
cooking the brakes.

262
00:09:24,639 --> 00:09:26,497
On long downhill grades,

263
00:09:26,497 --> 00:09:29,283
a heavy rig can overheat its brakes.

264
00:09:29,463 --> 00:09:33,388
The trailer manufacturers' association warns that prolonged

265
00:09:33,388 --> 00:09:36,115
braking can cause overheating and loss of

266
00:09:36,115 --> 00:09:37,578
braking effectiveness.

267
00:09:37,758 --> 00:09:39,394
That is when brakes fade,

268
00:09:39,394 --> 00:09:42,077
and stopping distance grows dramatically.

269
00:09:42,428 --> 00:09:44,497
The fix is to use the engine

270
00:09:44,497 --> 00:09:47,083
and transmission to help slow down.

271
00:09:47,263 --> 00:09:49,830
Most modern trucks have a tow or

272
00:09:49,830 --> 00:09:52,958
haul mode, and many have engine braking

273
00:09:52,958 --> 00:09:54,482
or exhaust braking,

274
00:09:54,482 --> 00:09:56,006
especially diesels.

275
00:09:56,186 --> 00:09:58,412
Shift to a lower gear before the

276
00:09:58,412 --> 00:10:00,220
descent, not halfway down,

277
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:03,281
and brake firmly and occasionally instead of

278
00:10:03,281 --> 00:10:04,463
riding the pedal.

279
00:10:04,814 --> 00:10:06,532
And check the trailer brakes.

280
00:10:06,712 --> 00:10:09,446
Many states require brakes on trailers above

281
00:10:09,446 --> 00:10:10,503
a certain weight,

282
00:10:10,503 --> 00:10:11,994
and the thresholds vary.

283
00:10:12,174 --> 00:10:14,381
A brake controller in the truck must

284
00:10:14,381 --> 00:10:16,342
be set for the trailer's weight.

285
00:10:16,522 --> 00:10:17,540
Too little gain,

286
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:19,576
and the truck does all the work.

287
00:10:19,756 --> 00:10:22,121
Too much, and the trailer wheels can

288
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:22,449
lock.

289
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:24,299
Mistake number seven:

290
00:10:24,299 --> 00:10:27,584
forgetting the safety chains and the breakaway

291
00:10:27,584 --> 00:10:28,012
cable.

292
00:10:28,192 --> 00:10:32,167
The trailer manufacturers' association says safety chains

293
00:10:32,167 --> 00:10:34,608
should be crossed under the tongue,

294
00:10:34,608 --> 00:10:36,630
connected, kept off the road,

295
00:10:36,630 --> 00:10:38,932
and given enough slack for turns.

296
00:10:39,112 --> 00:10:40,331
If the hitch fails,

297
00:10:40,331 --> 00:10:42,641
crossed chains can catch the tongue.

298
00:10:42,991 --> 00:10:44,426
And here is the twist:

299
00:10:44,426 --> 00:10:45,731
the breakaway cable.

300
00:10:45,911 --> 00:10:47,706
If the trailer separates,

301
00:10:47,706 --> 00:10:50,149
the cable pulls a pin that applies

302
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:51,658
the trailer's brakes.

303
00:10:51,838 --> 00:10:54,817
The association says to connect the breakaway

304
00:10:54,817 --> 00:10:56,208
lanyard to the truck,

305
00:10:56,208 --> 00:10:58,261
not to the safety chains or the

306
00:10:58,261 --> 00:10:58,989
ball mount.

307
00:10:59,169 --> 00:11:01,047
If it is attached to the wrong

308
00:11:01,047 --> 00:11:03,176
place, it may not activate when it

309
00:11:03,176 --> 00:11:03,802
is needed.

310
00:11:04,152 --> 00:11:06,516
Also make sure the coupler is fully

311
00:11:06,516 --> 00:11:07,867
latched on the ball,

312
00:11:07,867 --> 00:11:10,096
and the ball is the correct size.

313
00:11:10,276 --> 00:11:12,154
A ball that is too small can

314
00:11:12,154 --> 00:11:14,167
let the trailer pop off over a

315
00:11:14,167 --> 00:11:14,502
bump.

316
00:11:14,682 --> 00:11:16,975
The ball size is usually stamped on

317
00:11:16,975 --> 00:11:18,678
the top of the ball and on

318
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:19,988
the trailer coupler.

319
00:11:20,168 --> 00:11:21,689
Match them every time.

320
00:11:22,039 --> 00:11:23,705
Mistake number eight:

321
00:11:23,705 --> 00:11:25,371
ignoring maintenance.

322
00:11:25,551 --> 00:11:27,907
Towing is hard work for a truck.

323
00:11:28,087 --> 00:11:31,233
Many owner's manuals list towing as severe

324
00:11:31,233 --> 00:11:34,677
service, which usually means more frequent oil

325
00:11:34,677 --> 00:11:38,571
changes, transmission fluid changes and inspections.

326
00:11:38,751 --> 00:11:41,157
Skipping them can shorten the life of

327
00:11:41,157 --> 00:11:42,977
the transmission and engine.

328
00:11:43,328 --> 00:11:45,922
The transmission is often the part that

329
00:11:45,922 --> 00:11:46,787
suffers most.

330
00:11:46,967 --> 00:11:48,328
Heat is its enemy,

331
00:11:48,328 --> 00:11:50,822
and towing creates a lot of heat.

332
00:11:51,002 --> 00:11:54,478
Watch the transmission temperature if your truck

333
00:11:54,478 --> 00:11:56,723
shows it, use tow or haul mode,

334
00:11:56,723 --> 00:11:59,547
and follow the severe service schedule.

335
00:11:59,727 --> 00:12:02,938
A transmission repair can cost thousands of

336
00:12:02,938 --> 00:12:03,535
dollars.

337
00:12:03,885 --> 00:12:05,944
Here is a twist about the trailer

338
00:12:05,944 --> 00:12:06,381
itself.

339
00:12:06,561 --> 00:12:08,755
Trailers need maintenance too.

340
00:12:08,935 --> 00:12:10,964
Wheel bearings need grease,

341
00:12:10,964 --> 00:12:13,144
tires age even when they sit,

342
00:12:13,144 --> 00:12:16,075
and trailer brakes and lights wear out.

343
00:12:16,255 --> 00:12:18,898
A trailer that sits all winter can

344
00:12:18,898 --> 00:12:21,930
come back with dry bearings and cracked

345
00:12:21,930 --> 00:12:22,397
tires.

346
00:12:22,577 --> 00:12:24,891
Inspect it before the first trip of

347
00:12:24,891 --> 00:12:25,619
the season.

348
00:12:25,969 --> 00:12:27,965
And check the tires on the truck

349
00:12:27,965 --> 00:12:28,465
as well.

350
00:12:28,645 --> 00:12:30,311
When towing heavy loads,

351
00:12:30,311 --> 00:12:33,573
many manufacturers recommend a higher rear tire

352
00:12:33,573 --> 00:12:36,350
pressure, which is listed in the owner's

353
00:12:36,350 --> 00:12:38,432
manual or on the door sticker.

354
00:12:38,612 --> 00:12:42,555
Under-inflated tires overheat and wear quickly under

355
00:12:42,555 --> 00:12:43,465
heavy loads.

356
00:12:43,815 --> 00:12:45,232
Mistake number nine:

357
00:12:45,232 --> 00:12:47,216
the wrong truck for the job.

358
00:12:47,396 --> 00:12:50,062
A half-ton pickup can tow a lot,

359
00:12:50,062 --> 00:12:52,977
but a large travel trailer can push

360
00:12:52,977 --> 00:12:54,393
it to its limits,

361
00:12:54,393 --> 00:12:55,976
especially in wind.

362
00:12:56,156 --> 00:12:59,605
Heavy-duty trucks are built with stronger frames,

363
00:12:59,605 --> 00:13:01,787
brakes and axles for big loads.

364
00:13:01,967 --> 00:13:03,978
If you tow near the limit every

365
00:13:03,978 --> 00:13:06,314
weekend, the bigger truck may be the

366
00:13:06,314 --> 00:13:08,650
safer and cheaper choice in the long

367
00:13:08,650 --> 00:13:08,910
run.

368
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:11,106
Here is the twist about the cost.

369
00:13:11,286 --> 00:13:13,707
A bigger truck costs more to buy,

370
00:13:13,707 --> 00:13:15,248
and according to AAA,

371
00:13:15,248 --> 00:13:18,550
a half-ton pickup already costs about sixteen

372
00:13:18,550 --> 00:13:22,072
thousand, four hundred forty-nine dollars a year

373
00:13:22,072 --> 00:13:24,126
to own in twenty twenty-six.

374
00:13:24,306 --> 00:13:26,563
But a lighter truck pushed to its

375
00:13:26,563 --> 00:13:28,409
limits can wear out brakes,

376
00:13:28,409 --> 00:13:30,529
tires and transmissions faster.

377
00:13:30,709 --> 00:13:32,976
The cheapest truck is the one that

378
00:13:32,976 --> 00:13:34,842
does the job without strain.

379
00:13:35,193 --> 00:13:37,085
And engine choice matters.

380
00:13:37,265 --> 00:13:39,771
Diesels are known for strong torque and

381
00:13:39,771 --> 00:13:42,791
engine braking, which help with heavy trailers.

382
00:13:42,971 --> 00:13:46,470
Hybrids like the F-one-fifty PowerBoost can offer

383
00:13:46,470 --> 00:13:47,755
strong torque too.

384
00:13:47,935 --> 00:13:50,429
But with diesel at record prices in

385
00:13:50,429 --> 00:13:53,635
twenty twenty-six, the fuel math has changed.

386
00:13:53,815 --> 00:13:56,099
We break it down in our diesel

387
00:13:56,099 --> 00:13:58,459
versus gas versus hybrid video.

388
00:13:58,809 --> 00:14:01,525
There is also the electric question.

389
00:14:01,705 --> 00:14:04,027
Electric pickups have huge torque,

390
00:14:04,027 --> 00:14:07,033
but towing can cut their range dramatically,

391
00:14:07,033 --> 00:14:09,764
and charging with a trailer attached can

392
00:14:09,764 --> 00:14:12,565
be difficult at stations not designed for

393
00:14:12,565 --> 00:14:12,770
it.

394
00:14:12,950 --> 00:14:16,865
Ford ended production of the F-one-fifty Lightning

395
00:14:16,865 --> 00:14:18,588
in twenty twenty-five,

396
00:14:18,588 --> 00:14:20,624
according to Fox Business.

397
00:14:20,804 --> 00:14:22,905
For long-distance towing,

398
00:14:22,905 --> 00:14:25,342
most buyers still choose gas,

399
00:14:25,342 --> 00:14:26,771
diesel or hybrid.

400
00:14:27,122 --> 00:14:29,114
Now let's look at the most common

401
00:14:29,114 --> 00:14:32,253
towing situations, starting with the travel trailer.

402
00:14:32,433 --> 00:14:34,796
Travel trailers are tall and wide,

403
00:14:34,796 --> 00:14:37,159
which makes them catch wind like a

404
00:14:37,159 --> 00:14:37,507
sail.

405
00:14:37,687 --> 00:14:40,458
Even a trailer within your truck's ratings

406
00:14:40,458 --> 00:14:42,900
can feel unstable on a windy highway.

407
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:45,822
That is why weight distribution and sway

408
00:14:45,822 --> 00:14:48,838
control hitches are so popular with campers.

409
00:14:49,189 --> 00:14:51,058
And here is a camper twist.

410
00:14:51,238 --> 00:14:53,662
The weight printed on a new travel

411
00:14:53,662 --> 00:14:55,943
trailer is often its dry weight,

412
00:14:55,943 --> 00:14:57,582
without water, propane,

413
00:14:57,582 --> 00:14:58,866
batteries or gear.

414
00:14:59,046 --> 00:15:00,774
Once you load it for a trip,

415
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:02,935
the real weight can be much higher.

416
00:15:03,115 --> 00:15:05,586
Always plan using the loaded weight,

417
00:15:05,586 --> 00:15:07,783
or the trailer's maximum rating,

418
00:15:07,783 --> 00:15:09,431
not the brochure number.

419
00:15:09,781 --> 00:15:11,278
Water is heavy.

420
00:15:11,458 --> 00:15:14,132
Fresh water weighs about eight point three

421
00:15:14,132 --> 00:15:15,278
pounds per gallon.

422
00:15:15,458 --> 00:15:17,554
A full fresh water tank on a

423
00:15:17,554 --> 00:15:20,624
large trailer can add hundreds of pounds.

424
00:15:20,804 --> 00:15:23,417
Many campers travel with the tank nearly

425
00:15:23,417 --> 00:15:25,769
empty and fill it at the campground,

426
00:15:25,769 --> 00:15:27,989
which saves weight and fuel on the

427
00:15:27,989 --> 00:15:28,316
road.

428
00:15:28,666 --> 00:15:30,512
Next, the boat trailer.

429
00:15:30,692 --> 00:15:33,975
Boat trailers are often backed into water

430
00:15:33,975 --> 00:15:37,418
at ramps, which exposes bearings and brakes

431
00:15:37,418 --> 00:15:38,459
to water and,

432
00:15:38,459 --> 00:15:39,660
in some places,

433
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:40,061
salt.

434
00:15:40,241 --> 00:15:42,960
Rinse the trailer after saltwater use and

435
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,618
check the bearings often.

436
00:15:44,798 --> 00:15:47,206
A seized bearing can ruin a trip

437
00:15:47,206 --> 00:15:48,710
and damage the axle.

438
00:15:49,061 --> 00:15:51,162
And the ramp itself is a test.

439
00:15:51,342 --> 00:15:54,361
Steep, slippery boat ramps can be hard

440
00:15:54,361 --> 00:15:56,108
on a truck's traction,

441
00:15:56,108 --> 00:15:58,888
especially a two-wheel-drive truck.

442
00:15:59,068 --> 00:16:02,008
Four-wheel drive, good tires and a careful

443
00:16:02,008 --> 00:16:04,038
driver make a big difference.

444
00:16:04,218 --> 00:16:06,940
Practice launching on a quiet day before

445
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:08,641
the busy holiday weekend.

446
00:16:08,991 --> 00:16:11,080
Then the utility and car trailer.

447
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:14,185
These trailers are often loaded with heavy,

448
00:16:14,185 --> 00:16:17,042
compact cargo like equipment or a vehicle.

449
00:16:17,222 --> 00:16:18,604
Strapping matters.

450
00:16:18,784 --> 00:16:23,500
The trailer manufacturers' association recommends one tie-down

451
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:25,630
for every ten feet of cargo,

452
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:27,988
and at least two for any piece,

453
00:16:27,988 --> 00:16:29,585
regardless of length,

454
00:16:29,585 --> 00:16:32,704
secured low on the trailer when possible.

455
00:16:33,054 --> 00:16:36,153
And position the car or equipment carefully.

456
00:16:36,333 --> 00:16:37,335
On a car trailer,

457
00:16:37,335 --> 00:16:39,926
the vehicle's engine usually goes toward the

458
00:16:39,926 --> 00:16:41,988
front to keep enough tongue weight.

459
00:16:42,168 --> 00:16:44,641
Loading a car backward can shift weight

460
00:16:44,641 --> 00:16:46,924
behind the axle and make the trailer

461
00:16:46,924 --> 00:16:47,241
sway.

462
00:16:47,421 --> 00:16:49,866
A few feet forward or back can

463
00:16:49,866 --> 00:16:51,334
change everything.

464
00:16:51,684 --> 00:16:54,271
Then there are fifth wheel and gooseneck

465
00:16:54,271 --> 00:16:54,853
trailers.

466
00:16:55,033 --> 00:16:57,381
These hitch inside the truck bed,

467
00:16:57,381 --> 00:16:58,733
over the rear axle,

468
00:16:58,733 --> 00:17:01,366
which makes them much more stable for

469
00:17:01,366 --> 00:17:02,220
heavy loads.

470
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:04,121
But they put a lot of weight

471
00:17:04,121 --> 00:17:04,797
in the bed,

472
00:17:04,797 --> 00:17:07,195
so payload becomes even more important.

473
00:17:07,375 --> 00:17:10,141
Many fifth wheel owners use heavy-duty trucks

474
00:17:10,141 --> 00:17:11,125
for this reason.

475
00:17:11,475 --> 00:17:13,959
Here is a fifth wheel twist.

476
00:17:14,139 --> 00:17:17,049
Short-bed trucks can have very little clearance

477
00:17:17,049 --> 00:17:19,031
between the cab and the front of

478
00:17:19,031 --> 00:17:21,570
a fifth wheel trailer during tight turns.

479
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:24,470
Some owners use a sliding hitch to

480
00:17:24,470 --> 00:17:26,231
avoid hitting the cab.

481
00:17:26,411 --> 00:17:28,454
Check the clearance before you buy the

482
00:17:28,454 --> 00:17:28,884
trailer.

483
00:17:29,234 --> 00:17:31,583
Weather is the hidden factor in every

484
00:17:31,583 --> 00:17:32,345
towing trip.

485
00:17:32,525 --> 00:17:36,078
Rain, snow, ice and wind all reduce

486
00:17:36,078 --> 00:17:36,890
control.

487
00:17:37,070 --> 00:17:39,322
The best towers check the forecast for

488
00:17:39,322 --> 00:17:41,218
the whole route and are ready to

489
00:17:41,218 --> 00:17:42,225
wait out a storm.

490
00:17:42,405 --> 00:17:45,116
No trip is worth driving into dangerous

491
00:17:45,116 --> 00:17:47,270
crosswinds with a tall trailer.

492
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:49,408
And plan rest stops.

493
00:17:49,588 --> 00:17:51,953
Towing is tiring because you have to

494
00:17:51,953 --> 00:17:53,071
concentrate more.

495
00:17:53,251 --> 00:17:56,160
Stopping every couple of hours lets you

496
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:58,697
rest and also walk around the rig:

497
00:17:58,697 --> 00:17:59,891
check the hitch,

498
00:17:59,891 --> 00:18:02,502
the chains, the lights and feel the

499
00:18:02,502 --> 00:18:04,741
trailer hubs for unusual heat,

500
00:18:04,741 --> 00:18:07,128
which can be an early warning of

501
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:08,471
a bearing problem.

502
00:18:08,822 --> 00:18:11,260
Finally, think about insurance.

503
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:14,588
Your auto policy may cover liability when

504
00:18:14,588 --> 00:18:17,199
you tow, but damage to the trailer

505
00:18:17,199 --> 00:18:19,811
itself may need separate coverage.

506
00:18:19,991 --> 00:18:22,675
Campers and boats often need their own

507
00:18:22,675 --> 00:18:23,311
policies.

508
00:18:23,491 --> 00:18:26,165
Ask your insurer before your first trip,

509
00:18:26,165 --> 00:18:27,636
not after an accident.

510
00:18:27,986 --> 00:18:29,472
And rent before you buy.

511
00:18:29,652 --> 00:18:31,179
If you are new to towing,

512
00:18:31,179 --> 00:18:33,317
renting a trailer for a weekend can

513
00:18:33,317 --> 00:18:35,149
teach you a lot about how your

514
00:18:35,149 --> 00:18:36,432
truck handles a load.

515
00:18:36,612 --> 00:18:38,973
You will quickly learn whether your truck

516
00:18:38,973 --> 00:18:41,910
feels comfortable, whether you need better mirrors,

517
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:43,925
and whether a bigger truck might be

518
00:18:43,925 --> 00:18:46,114
worth it before you spend thousands on

519
00:18:46,114 --> 00:18:46,689
a trailer.

520
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,373
Let's add some practical habits.

521
00:18:49,553 --> 00:18:52,071
Practice backing up in an empty parking

522
00:18:52,071 --> 00:18:53,814
lot before your first trip.

523
00:18:53,994 --> 00:18:55,968
Use a spotter when backing.

524
00:18:56,148 --> 00:18:58,517
Plan fuel stops where a truck and

525
00:18:58,517 --> 00:18:59,666
trailer can fit.

526
00:18:59,846 --> 00:19:02,736
And give yourself extra space around other

527
00:19:02,736 --> 00:19:06,176
vehicles, because everything takes longer when you

528
00:19:06,176 --> 00:19:06,452
tow.

529
00:19:06,802 --> 00:19:09,437
And use the technology your truck has.

530
00:19:09,617 --> 00:19:13,066
Many modern pickups offer trailer backup assist,

531
00:19:13,066 --> 00:19:16,659
trailer cameras, blind spot monitoring that covers

532
00:19:16,659 --> 00:19:20,252
the trailer, and trailer tire pressure monitoring.

533
00:19:20,432 --> 00:19:23,067
These features can make towing easier and

534
00:19:23,067 --> 00:19:25,188
safer, but they only help if they

535
00:19:25,188 --> 00:19:27,630
are set up correctly for your trailer.

536
00:19:27,980 --> 00:19:30,035
Here is one last twist.

537
00:19:30,215 --> 00:19:32,606
The most dangerous moment is often not

538
00:19:32,606 --> 00:19:33,361
the highway.

539
00:19:33,541 --> 00:19:35,566
It is the first and last few

540
00:19:35,566 --> 00:19:39,543
minutes: hitching, unhitching and leaving the driveway.

541
00:19:39,723 --> 00:19:42,401
Most mistakes happen when people are in

542
00:19:42,401 --> 00:19:42,951
a hurry.

543
00:19:43,131 --> 00:19:45,828
A slow, careful routine at the start

544
00:19:45,828 --> 00:19:48,225
of every trip is the best safety

545
00:19:48,225 --> 00:19:49,423
system you have.

546
00:19:49,774 --> 00:19:52,072
So here is your towing checklist.

547
00:19:52,252 --> 00:19:53,813
One: check lights,

548
00:19:53,813 --> 00:19:57,628
tires, brakes and recalls before every trip.

549
00:19:57,808 --> 00:20:00,741
Two: know your payload and every weight

550
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:01,268
rating.

551
00:20:01,448 --> 00:20:03,781
Three: balance the tongue weight.

552
00:20:03,961 --> 00:20:06,953
Four: stay calm in sway and slow

553
00:20:06,953 --> 00:20:07,421
down.

554
00:20:07,601 --> 00:20:10,378
Five: use the engine to brake on

555
00:20:10,378 --> 00:20:10,898
hills.

556
00:20:11,078 --> 00:20:13,514
And six: cross the chains and connect

557
00:20:13,514 --> 00:20:15,687
the breakaway cable to the truck.

558
00:20:16,038 --> 00:20:18,402
We put a printable towing checklist and

559
00:20:18,402 --> 00:20:20,464
a full guide to choosing the right

560
00:20:20,464 --> 00:20:22,768
truck for your trailer into the Twenty

561
00:20:22,768 --> 00:20:24,768
Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

562
00:20:24,948 --> 00:20:27,169
The link is in the description and

563
00:20:27,169 --> 00:20:28,605
in the pinned comment.

564
00:20:28,785 --> 00:20:31,096
Subscribe for the next video:

565
00:20:31,096 --> 00:20:33,646
diesel versus gas versus hybrid,

566
00:20:33,646 --> 00:20:36,355
